{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S31-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d7c6615990e0fc3462f38c8d78fde519c25a280bb7c97b6e487399f4979b924c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 assigns familiar washing roles, but A5's 'supervise your replacement' abandons the old division of work.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to the dishwasher; A5 responds specifically to B4's drying capability.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 offer practical relief while A keeps finding B a role.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds supervision, but weakens the established insistence on familiar habits.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's two distinctive mugs and 'I'll wash; you dry' establish an immediately playable domestic routine.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'while it learns' is compact personification tied to the appliance.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 73\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your chipped mug, my ugly mug. I'll wash; you dry.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I bought a dishwasher. Put them in.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yours on the left, mine on the right. Have you got our tea towel?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It dries them too. We can sit down together.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. Your end of the sofa, mine here. Pass the tea towel; you always fold while I tell you about work.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A immediately organizes shared activity through familiar shorthand and inherited habits, carrying those habits into changed circumstances.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fear of replacement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 establishes habitual roles, but original A5 emphasizes replacement; revised A5 instead carries their familiar division of activity onto the sofa.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a preserves domestic coordination through B's helpful modernization; b preserves a friendship's arrival signal across communication methods.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised the whole interaction within the existing domestic setting because the original ending drifted toward replacement anxiety. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 preserve familiar divisions), logic 5 (B4's invitation to sit produces the sofa routine), relationship 4 (B offers shared rest), heightening 4 (A5 extends habit into resting), specificity 5 (A1's mugs and roles), brevity/wit 4 (A5's towel folding earns its place). Total 92. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words; hard gates pass. No runtime or live testing performed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The sofa routine introduces another shared habit; actors must make it sound remembered rather than newly invented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S31-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"6e2fc405a3e1c2cf6297f3fe6ffff52aa2c690b855d6ccd03c9be63745c7a90b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes 'our usual walk'; A3 and A5 preserve the two-knock signal through successive changes.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's doorbell becomes A3's two rings; B4's texting request becomes A5's two written knocks.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B wants a less intrusive arrival and then advance notice, changing A's method twice.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 carries the physical signal into text, increasing the persistence of the habit.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a familiar walking companion at a window; B2's moved doorbell is slightly unusual.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'I'll text two knocks' compactly transforms B4's proposed solution.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've knocked twice on your window. Ready for our usual walk?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I moved the doorbell so you wouldn't need to.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Lovely. I'll ring it twice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could you text first?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll text two knocks. You'll know it's me.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A immediately organizes shared activity through familiar shorthand and inherited habits, carrying those habits into changed circumstances.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Resistance to technology.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 accepts the doorbell and A5 accepts texting; what survives is the familiar two-knock signal, not the old technology.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's domestic division of activity, b adapts an identifying signal while accommodating B's requests.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly. Fresh internal rereading confirms fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 preserve the signal), logic 5 (each new medium comes from B), relationship 4 (B seeks less intrusion), heightening 4 (A5 translates knocking into text), specificity 4 (A1 establishes the walk), brevity/wit 5 ('text two knocks'). Total 92. B4 directly causes A5's new expression. Hard gates pass; no rewrite, runtime validation, or live test claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Texting two knocks could become merely cute unless A treats it as the obvious established procedure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S32-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"225f8b94498cceac8c9e3d8cab0d97b072fe6e803e29bc9498ca2b05fc8dd18e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 totals past lifts and an umbrella; A3 credits yesterday's coffee against only part of the journey.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 values B2's coffee; A5 answers B4's exact 'no trouble' assurance by separating trouble from the favor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B offers evidence of repayment, then challenges A's terms using A's previous assurance.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds a separate category of debt when B tries to cancel the obligation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a lift home and concrete shared debts, though their relationship remains implicit.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Trouble is charged separately' follows the accounting logic, though it has a polished punchline shape.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll drive you home. That makes three lifts and a borrowed umbrella.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I bought you coffee yesterday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which covers the first roundabout.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You said the lift was no trouble.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Correct. Trouble is charged separately.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts current requests and previous kindnesses into an accumulating account of obligations and repayments.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Competitive scorekeeping.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 treats coffee as partial repayment and A5 distinguishes charge categories; A seeks an outstanding balance, not a winning rank.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"A supplies a favor while minimizing B's repayment; b collects a favor by enlarging the value of A's earlier help.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 account for favors), logic 5 (B4's assurance causes A5's charge distinction), relationship 4 (B contests the balance), heightening 4 (A5 adds a charge category), specificity 4 (lift and umbrella), brevity/wit 4 (compact accounting tag). Total 90. Hard gates pass; this is internal model review only.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The charging language should remain interpersonal bookkeeping rather than establish an actual taxi fare.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S32-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"468c23fb6da752107328bb426c8930a2d53c9b09bfd6d9210dda3b75f7af50f7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 calls in March's shift coverage; A3 and A5 keep comparing the requested work with that earlier favor.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's 'one afternoon' prompts A3's 'only six small plants'; B4's tree prompts A5's overtime.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B disputes both the size of the debt and A's description of the watering job.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 reveals extra historical labor precisely when B reveals extra present labor.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes coworkers negotiating plant care, though the duration of watering is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's five-word overtime claim neatly answers B4's tree without explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you water my plants? I covered your shift in March.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That was one afternoon.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And these are only six small plants.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"One is a tree.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The shift included overtime.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts current requests and previous kindnesses into an accumulating account of obligations and repayments.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary bargaining over workload.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 and A5 use an old shift and its overtime as credit against today's unrelated plant care.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"B uses remembered labor to demand repayment, whereas a performs new labor and discounts repayment already received.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (March's favor governs the request), logic 5 (B4's larger plant causes A5's larger credit), relationship 4 (B disputes scope), heightening 4 (overtime increases the claim), specificity 4 (coworkers and plants), brevity/wit 5 (tree/overtime exchange). Total 92. Hard gates pass; no independent or live approval claimed.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The tree's extra burden is assumed rather than explained; its size should be readily imaginable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S33-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"fa551601cf362be41f94894ad2728c49c3efb4a19643002be3c99aed964ab6ca\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an unsolicited reminder; A3 adds a reminder to check reminders; A5 recalls B's lost phone.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's calendar, and A5 challenges B4's alerts through the device needed to receive them.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B claims practical independence through a calendar and alerts; A supplies a remembered reason for doubt.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands responsibility from remembering the appointment to remembering where the reminder device is.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives a dentist appointment tomorrow, though 'I've reminded you' sounds slightly retrospective.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's two questions efficiently expose a further dependency without explaining the card.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've reminded you about the dentist tomorrow.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's in my calendar.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. I'll remind you to check the calendar.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It sends alerts.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"To which phone? The one you asked me to find?\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies unsolicited reminders and treats keeping track of another person's memory failures as an established personal responsibility.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General caretaking martyrdom.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 specifically monitors checking the calendar and A5 specifically remembers the missing alert device; the burden concerns remembering.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"A challenges electronic reminders through remembered dependence; b changes a physical reminder's placement after learning why it was missed.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 anticipate forgetting), logic 5 (B4 alerts require A5's phone), relationship 4 (B offers independence), heightening 4 (A5 exposes another memory dependency), specificity 4 (dentist tomorrow), brevity/wit 4 (short phone challenge). Total 90. Hard gates pass; review remains internal.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 supplies a new past fact; it should land as familiar shared history rather than a surprise accusation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S33-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3127818a4a42da935ff3b7dd25c955aeaf68d1f926046e86c5d569e170e04c48\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 writes an unsolicited bin reminder on breakfast; A5 takes responsibility for improving its placement.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 uses B4's lack of hunger, but A3 treats an uneaten banana as evidence that B forgot bin day.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B asserts remembering and gives a credible explanation for not eating the reminder.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends reminder management to B's coffee routine.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's breakfast banana makes the household reminder immediately visible and playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's coffee-machine solution follows the breakfast premise, although the banana inference needs repair.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 83\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Bin day tomorrow. I've written it on your breakfast banana.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I don't eat breakfast on Thursdays.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Right. Another thing for me to remember. I'll put it by your coffee.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll set a reminder on my phone. You can stop writing on food.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Charge it tonight. I'll leave that reminder on your dinner.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A supplies unsolicited reminders and treats keeping track of another person's memory failures as an established personal responsibility.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Eccentric household organization.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 explicitly shoulders 'another thing for me to remember'; A5 anticipates B forgetting the phone's charge.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Unlike a's verbal challenge to device reliability, b keeps relocating written reminders around B's daily routines.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the original household setting to remove A3's unsupported inference. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A3 names the burden; A5 adds an unsolicited reminder), logic 5 (B2 redirects placement; B4's phone causes charging advice), relationship 4 (B proposes relief), heightening 4 (the replacement system itself needs A's reminder), specificity 5 (banana, coffee, dinner), brevity/wit 4 (food returns causally). Total 92. Under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The return to writing on food is conspicuous; sincerity depends on A prioritizing reminder reliability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S34-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"300c1fd7ef84253ef0b1404a47d197da5cbe468a39e50f0d0c6c16b94af705b5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 compares effort and A5 invokes a stair count, but A3 says 'keep things fair' rather than clearly preserve a lead.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A3's carrying one bag twice lacks a practical meaning; B4's joint trip would not clearly erase a stair count.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers to take the heavy bag and B4 offers cooperation, both credible attempts to help.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 introduces stair scoring, but the connection to B4's proposal is muddled.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes shopping at stairs; A3's double trip is difficult to stage coherently.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 is short, but 'erase the stair count' substitutes an unclear scoring claim for an earned turn.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 64\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I carried the heavier shopping bag again. That's three trips to your two.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll take both bags upstairs. Then we're even.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll come too. Someone has to open the doors.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They're already propped open. You can rest.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll close them behind you. Two bags, three doors. I'm still ahead.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A measures ordinary contributions as a running competition and changes the measure to preserve a personal lead.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking fair repayment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 protects a count; revised A5 explicitly claims 'I'm still ahead' rather than asking B to repay a favor.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"A invents additional work when B offers equality; b changes how effort is valued when B presents a stronger contribution.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the shopping-and-stairs setting to make each physical task intelligible. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A1/A5 explicitly defend a lead), logic 5 (B4 removes opening doors, causing A5 to count closing them), relationship 4 (B offers relief and equality), heightening 4 (A5 changes units to retain victory), specificity 4 (bags and doors are playable), brevity/wit 4 (the final calculation earns the joke). Total 90. Under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's comparison of bags with doors is deliberately self-serving, not consistent arithmetic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S34-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a072f221d4791cef0be694b1d7b6550bd85d2d26f9ab63055cae2075fef32562\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 discounts B's evening effort, but A1/A5 do not make the running lead especially explicit.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's hour; A5 uses B4's upstairs address but 'sacrificed a shorter commute' is conceptually unclear.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B counters A's early arrival with late work and then challenges A's claimed difficulty.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 attempts to convert convenience into sacrifice without identifying what was sacrificed.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes setup work and arrival time; B4 supplies a concrete shared building.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"The final phrase is economical but needs decoding before the competitive logic can land.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'm ten minutes early to set up. That's twice this week I've beaten you here.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I stayed an hour late yesterday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You were already awake. Mine involved leaving bed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You live upstairs. I took two buses.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. You were committed after the first bus. I could have gone back to bed at every step. Count those.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A measures ordinary contributions as a running competition and changes the measure to preserve a personal lead.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Defensiveness about doing too little.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A1 claims two victories and A5 demands a count of resisted opportunities to return to bed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"B argues for superior sacrifice by revaluing convenience; a adds physical tasks to outscore B's helpful contribution.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised within the original setup setting to explain how A converts proximity into greater sacrifice. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A1 claims a running lead; A5 demands another count), logic 4 (B4's buses and upstairs address supply A5's comparison), relationship 4 (B asserts substantial effort), heightening 4 (A5 counts resisted temptations), specificity 5 (setup, buses, upstairs bed), brevity/wit 4 (the faulty valuation is intelligible). Total 88. Under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 is more verbally elaborate than a's ending and requires a clear, matter-of-fact delivery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S35-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"cc412f53cb9aec8ff8f55de4ba04f0578c1496acdd0ed0d47008bdd0270490f3\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 disguises a request for directions as checking changes; A3 pretends B's answer confirms A's existing knowledge.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 appropriates B2's counter information; A5 explains away the wrong direction revealed in B4.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B first supplies useful information, then refuses A's pretence by identifying the toilet-bound mistake.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 upgrades a navigation mistake into an inspection of signage for other people.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a forms counter naturally, though the institution is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Good. You remember' efficiently reverses who supposedly needed help.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which counter takes these forms? Just checking they've not moved it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's been counter three for years.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. You remember.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You were heading for the toilets.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Checking whether the signs still mislead newcomers.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A extracts practical knowledge from B while presenting that dependence as verification of knowledge A already possesses.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General bluffing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks this B for the working counter and A3 repackages B2's actual answer as a successful knowledge check.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"A covers an exposed navigation error; b will keep acquiring successive pieces of a routine through supposed confirmation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained exactly. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A1/A3 hide information dependence), logic 5 (B4's toilets cause A5's signage excuse), relationship 4 (B helps then exposes), heightening 4 (A5 claims inspection), specificity 4 (forms and counter three), brevity/wit 4 ('Good. You remember'). Total 90. Hard gates pass; no improvement invented.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 shifts briefly from using B's knowledge to defending the resulting bluff, but stays within the established behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S35-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"d5ee0d4ef8ffa9f63cbabc68f1065523e00a55c9ffe12407b4fb251086dc3bcf\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 disguises ignorance as a systems test, but A5 openly asks which shed without much cover.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's challenge; A5 acknowledges the red key but introduces unexplained uncertainty about which shed.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B challenges once and then gives a key color; B's practical purpose remains thin.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 broadens ignorance from key to shed but weakens the pretence of independent competence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a shed key but not why they need entry; A5 makes the physical situation less clear.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'whether our systems agree' is a compact face-saving tactic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"We're opening the allotment shed today. Pass me the key you'd use; I'll check it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The red one. The lock sticks unless you lift the handle.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, that method. How high do you lift it? Just comparing.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"All the way. I'll go start the watering.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Wait. Which tap are you using? I should check you're following the usual order.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A extracts practical knowledge from B while presenting that dependence as verification of knowledge A already possesses.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Openly asking for help.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 requests a precise handle movement under 'Just comparing'; A5 disguises another question as checking B's procedure.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"B sustains dependence on a helpful coworker who is about to leave; a defends competence after B exposes a wrong turn.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Introduced an explicit allotment-opening setting to ground the shed routine. Fresh internal second pass: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 conceal requests as checks), logic 5 (B2's handle prompts A3; B4's departure to water prompts A5's tap question), relationship 4 (B wants to begin work), heightening 4 (A needs B for another stage), specificity 5 (red key, sticking lock, tap), brevity/wit 4 (procedural cover remains compact). Total 92. Under 75 words; hard gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The allotment may have several taps; the scene leaves their arrangement open rather than requiring an actual system.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S36-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8fd9e8f08eef63e896f981cdbea1aca0e3af27fe6e7c698e0b066e6865982ecb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 makes the sock a recurring chapter; A3 invokes last month's three days; A5 anticipates the old promise.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 repeats and contests B2's 'just now'; A5 casts B4's proposed cleanup as another familiar stage.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B explains the fresh accident and offers immediate repair, which A treats through shared history.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands from a recurring sock to B's recurring promises of personal reform.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 provides a playable sock on stairs and A3 a concrete previous duration.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'just now lasted three days' earns its wit from B2's exact explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"There's a sock on the stairs. We've reached this chapter again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I dropped it just now.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And last month 'just now' lasted three days.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'